{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788582627415995001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"culm-auxiliary-smelts","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":1,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"8a1b0f9fe842fa4e12d12249d378cbe3a110fbd8d30d4452c5b2ffbd36c98675","event_uuid":"fb3749ed-0d76-4e45-a36d-a97954a097d2","position":{"commit_sha":"6f4154ad9b6b23283ccbecdb12214ab1353cb832","position":"1788571064692206001-fb3749ed-0d76-4e45-a36d-a97954a097d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788571064692206001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## The defect\n\n`infra/scripts/install-observability.sh:12` deploys ONLY the probe:\n\n```\ninstall -m 0755 \"${SCRIPT_DIR}/observability.sh\" /usr/local/bin/rebar-observability.sh\n```\n\nBut `observability.sh` resolves its two cap scripts as **siblings of its own path**\n(`:290` and `:458`):\n\n```\nDOCKER_CAP_SH=\"${DOCKER_CAP_SH:-$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)/docker-storage-cap.sh}\"\n```\n\nSo the deployed probe at `/usr/local/bin/rebar-observability.sh` looks for\n`docker-storage-cap.sh` and `journald-cap.sh` in `/usr/local/bin/`, where the installer never put\nthem. Verified on the live host: **neither existed there.**\n\n## Consequences, both observed\n\n**1. Three metrics silently never publish.** `docker_storage_used_percent`,\n`docker_buildkit_cache_used_percent` and `journal_used_percent` are each gated on a budget read\nfrom `--print-env`. With the cap scripts unreachable the reads fail, so the metrics publish\nNOTHING. That is the correct silence-not-zero behaviour firing for an incorrect reason — the caps\nwere installed and readable ON DISK, just not from where the probe looked.\n\n**2. `journal_cap_in_effect` is pinned at a FALSE 0 — this is the serious half.** Unlike the\npercent metrics it publishes UNGATED, so an unreachable `journald-cap.sh` yields 0 rather than\nsilence. `rebar-journal-cap-not-in-effect` would therefore have fired **forever, with the cap\ngenuinely in force on the host.** An alarm asserting a false negative indefinitely is worse than a\nmissing alarm: it trains its reader to ignore it, and it does so while the thing it watches is\nactually healthy.\n\n## How it was found\n\nDuring an operator-authorised cap install on 2026-09-05. Installing both caps was NOT sufficient to\nmake the metrics publish; the scripts had to be placed at `/usr/local/bin/` by hand before\n`docker_storage_used_percent` (63.0), `docker_buildkit_cache_used_percent` (100.0),\n`journal_used_percent` (56.0) appeared and `journal_cap_in_effect` flipped 0 -> 1.\n\nA second, related deployment gap surfaced in the same pass: **`journald-cap.sh` did not exist on the\nhost at all.** `/opt/rebar` is a deployed non-git tree predating commit `e510c64`, and nothing had\ndelivered the new script. It was copied over SHA-verified. That is adjacent to\n`octahedral-auburn-sunfish` (5246-2ec0-1fa6-4637), which records that neither cap script appears in\nany of `autodeploy.sh`'s `*_PATHS` — so a commit changing a cap signals nothing.\n\n## Why this belongs with tonight's recurring class\n\nThe probe reports a value it cannot actually measure, and the failure presents as a healthy-looking\nnumber. Same family as: a drift gate blinded by whitespace before `plan` ever ran; a CI job casting\na passing vote without executing; a test passing vacuously because a monkeypatched TMPDIR was inert;\na cap reporting itself \"in effect\" after a SIGHUP that does not apply it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 - `install-observability.sh` deploys every script `observability.sh` resolves at runtime,\n      or `observability.sh` resolves them from a location the installer guarantees. Either\n      direction is acceptable; the invariant is that a deployed probe can reach every dependency it\n      names.\n- [ ] AC2 - Defect-seeded: with a cap script absent from the deploy location, a test FAILS. Removing\n      it from the installer must turn that test RED.\n- [ ] AC3 - `journal_cap_in_effect` distinguishes \"the cap is not in effect\" from \"I could not\n      determine whether the cap is in effect\". Publishing a confident 0 for an unreadable input is\n      the defect; silence or a distinct value is the fix. Coordinate with the probe's own stated\n      contract that a probe which cannot measure publishes NOTHING rather than a plausible value\n      (`observability.sh:280`, `:487`).\n- [ ] AC4 - A check catches a deployed probe whose resolved dependencies are missing, so this is\n      detected at deploy time rather than by an operator noticing metrics are absent.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nNot changing what the caps do. Not fixing the autodeploy `*_PATHS` gap\n(`octahedral-auburn-sunfish`). Not restarting Docker.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5fb0-89ab-4466-41cc","ticket_type":"bug","title":"install-observability.sh deploys only the probe, so observability.sh cannot reach the cap scripts it resolves as siblings — three metrics stay silent and journal_cap_in_effect publishes a false 0 forever","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["fb3749ed-0d76-4e45-a36d-a97954a097d2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788582627415995001,"uuid":"f3c788c7-9e94-4a23-93f2-537bb5c4c184"}